From: rnsbox <rnsbox@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] riscv: dts: sophgo: sg2000-milkv-duo-s: reclock the uarts for exact 2 Mbaud SLIP

The board dts inherited the mainline uart nodes with the SoC default
clk_cam0_200 rate (25 MHz), so the HaLow SLIP link could not exceed
1,562,500 baud. Reclock disppll 1188 -> 768 MHz and clk_cam0_200 ->
disppll/8 = 96 MHz in of_clk_init(), before the 8250 probes; 2 Mbaud
becomes exact (96M/16/3) and uart0 stays at 115200 (+0.16%).

Enable uart1 for the SLIP modem. The mainline pinctrl driver does not
model the XGPIOA[28]/[29] pads, so the fmux is set by S31slip at boot
(same function-1 values the vendor u-boot writes); the runtime path
works without depending on a kernel pinctrl change.

---
diff --git a/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/sg2000-milkv-duo-s.dts b/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/sg2000-milkv-duo-s.dts
index 9fa77ba..d87e7f2 100644
--- a/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/sg2000-milkv-duo-s.dts
+++ b/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/sg2000-milkv-duo-s.dts
@@ -242,3 +242,18 @@
 	dr_mode = "peripheral";
 	status = "okay";
 };
+
+/* RNSBox: reclock disppll 1188 -> 768 MHz and clk_cam0_200 -> disppll/8 =
+ * 96 MHz in of_clk_init(), before the 8250 probes, so the modem's factory
+ * 2 Mbaud is exact (96M/16/3). The mainline pinctrl driver does not model
+ * the UART1 pads; S31slip sets the XGPIOA[28]/[29] fmux itself at boot.
+ */
+&clk {
+	assigned-clocks = <&clk CLK_DISPPLL>, <&clk CLK_CAM0_200>;
+	assigned-clock-parents = <0>, <&clk CLK_DISPPLL>;
+	assigned-clock-rates = <768000000>, <96000000>;
+};
+
+&uart1 {
+	status = "okay";
+};
-- 
